# This file must sit at the build context root, which for the backend *and* the chat client is
# the repository root -- both reference RedePanda.Contracts. Excluding bin/ and obj/ is not just
# about image size: copying the host's obj/ into the build would overwrite the restore performed
# inside the container with an asset file that points at host paths, and `dotnet publish
# --no-restore` then fails on missing packages.
**/bin/
**/obj/

**/.vs/
**/.vscode/
**/.idea/
.git/
.github/
.direnv/
/result

deploy/
scripts/
tests/
RedePanda-kafka-docker/
# src/RedePanda.ChatClient/ is deliberately NOT excluded: it has its own image now, built from
# this same context. It costs the backend build a few kilobytes of context and nothing in the
# resulting image, which copies only what it names.
#
# The frontend stays out: its context is its own directory, not this one.
src/RedePanda.Frontend/

*.md
*.png
**/Dockerfile
.dockerignore
.envrc
flake.nix
flake.lock
